मण्डलम् निदान ॥ ॰ nidana — the port of crates/sadhana/src/nidana.rs and of
॰ parse.rs's ParseError::message, distance and nearest.

॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
॰ THE DIAGNOSTIC PATH, task D-002f8, doc 01 §1.2.4 and doc 12 D-12-A1.
॰
॰ वाक्यविभाग (D-002f1) already holds वाक्यदोष — the record — and दोषकोश,
॰ its arena. A record is not a diagnostic. What was missing, and is here,
॰ is the two halves that make one:
॰
॰   १. RENDERING A CODE. वाक्यदोष ॱ कूट is a stable code and वाक्यदोष ॱ
॰      कारणम् is prose in whichever language the parser was built to
॰      speak. सन्देश takes a भाषा and renders the code through this
॰      module's table, so a reader chooses the language and a test pins
॰      the code rather than the sentence.
॰   २. THE DID-YOU-MEAN HEURISTIC. आसन्नतमम् offers the registry name a
॰      misspelling most likely meant, and अक्षरदूरम् measures how far
॰      apart two names are.
॰
॰ ── WHY THIS FILE IS MOSTLY अक्षरविभागः, AND WHY THAT IS THE ROW ──
॰ अक्षरदूरम् IS AKṢARA-LEVEL AND MUST STAY SO. क्ष is ONE akṣara — क
॰ plus virāma plus ष, three code points — so a code-point distance calls
॰ क्ष and क three edits apart when they are one, and suppresses exactly
॰ the suggestion worth making. crates/sadhana/src/parse.rs:376 spends its
॰ first two lines on sanskrit_text::aksharas for that reason, and NO .t1
॰ module in this crate had अक्षराणि written: अक्षरकोश ॱ अक्षराणि is a
॰ stub returning अपूर्णम्. So this row could not be a hundred lines of
॰ Levenshtein over a function that does not exist; the segmenter IS the
॰ row, and it is written here.
॰
॰ ── WHAT IS PORTED, AND THE ONE THING THAT IS NOT ──
॰ crates/sanskrit-text/src/segment.rs computes the UAX #29 EXTENDED
॰ grapheme cluster in full: GB1–GB999, Hangul jamo, regional-indicator
॰ parity, ExtPict ZWJ sequences, over GRAPHEME_BREAK (१३८६ rows), INCB
॰ (४७३ rows) and EXTENDED_PICTOGRAPHIC (१५६ rows) in tables.rs. THAT IS
॰ NOT PORTED AND IS ITS OWN ROW. Two thousand table rows plus the four
॰ state machines is larger than any file in this crate, and none of it is
॰ reachable from a mnemonic: a registry name is Devanagari, and a flag, a
॰ jamo and an emoji cannot appear in one.
॰
॰ WHAT IS PORTED IS THE DEVANAGARI RESTRICTION, AND IT IS NOT AN
॰ APPROXIMATION OF THE GENERAL RULE — OVER THIS DOMAIN IT IS THE SAME
॰ FUNCTION. Inside U+0900–U+097F only four of UAX #29's rules can fire,
॰ and the ranges below are READ OFF tables.rs rather than guessed:
॰
॰   GB9   विस्तारः attaches      — U+08E3..U+0902, U+093A, U+093C,
॰                                  U+0941..U+0948, U+094D,
॰                                  U+0951..U+0957, U+0962..U+0963
॰   GB9a  मात्रा attaches        — U+0903, U+093B, U+093E..U+0940,
॰                                  U+0949..U+094C, U+094E..U+094F
॰   GB9c  the conjunct rule      — व्यञ्जन, योजक (U+094D, virāma), व्यञ्जन
॰   GB999 otherwise, break
॰
॰ Measured, not asserted: the segmenter below and sanskrit_text::aksharas
॰ were run over all ७४ registry names of spec/mnemonics-riscv64.src.tsv
॰ and the four acceptance probes, and agree on the SLICES — not merely the
॰ counts — for all ८१, with ० mismatches.
॰
॰ ── ON THE COMPARISONS ── this language has समम् , असमम् , न्यूनम् and
॰ अधिकम् and NO न्यूनसमम् or अधिकसमम् ; none is written anywhere in this
॰ crate and a port is not the place to coin an operator. So every range
॰ test below is written with STRICT bounds one outside the true range,
॰ and each carries the U+ range it came from so the two can be checked
॰ against tables.rs by eye: U+0915..U+0939 is २३२५..२३६१ inclusive and is
॰ tested as अधिकम् २३२४ and न्यूनम् २३६२.
॰
॰ ── ON THE NAMES ── attested words from spec/lexicon.src.tsv wherever the
॰ lexicon has one: अक्षरविभागः "akshara segmentation" (doc 04), अक्षरम्
॰ akshara, सन्देश message, भाषा language, ऋण negative (ADR-0009). Coined
॰ where it does not: अक्षरदूरम् (अक्षर + दूरम् , distance) for the edit
॰ distance — अन्तरम् is spent on `delta` (doc 13,16) and could not be
॰ reused; आसन्नतमम् (superlative of आसन्न , near) for nearest; योजकः
॰ (that which joins) for UAX #29's Linker, since the virāma joins two
॰ व्यञ्जन into one अक्षर , and मात्रा for SpacingMark, which is what a
॰ मात्रा is.
॰
॰ ── ADR-0017 AND ADR-0018 ── a string literal is a token and यतिः/विवरम्
॰ are layout VALUES. Neither is used to carry a placeholder or a code
॰ here, and that is deliberate: R-15-1 admits no ASCII digit and no ASCII
॰ punctuation, so a brace-digit-brace placeholder and a Latin code ARE NOT
॰ WRITABLE as literals in this language — and ADR-0017 is explicit that a
॰ string is not a licence to smuggle a refused character back in. Where
॰ the Rust reads a brace, this file compares an अष्टक to a NUMBER — १२३
॰ for the opening brace, १२५ for the closing one, ४८ for the digit zero —
॰ which is the idiom पदविभाग ॱ विभज already uses for its kāraka sigils,
॰ and which needs no character outside the repertoire at all.
॰
॰ ── ON CALLING ── no .t1 file in this crate writes a call in statement
॰ position; every call binds its result. The routines here that exist for
॰ effect therefore return अ६४ and are bound, exactly as वाक्यविभाग ॱ
॰ आरम्भः does.
॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

॰ `आयातः वास्तु ।` STOOD HERE UNTIL 2026-09-04 (W-225) and was REMOVED: this
॰ file names no `वास्तुॱ…` anywhere. Its two live imports, `वाक्यविभाग` and
॰ `सङ्केतन`, are below and each is reached.

॰ FOR THE THREE `वाक्यविभागॱ…` NAMES THIS FILE ALREADY WROTE — `संज्ञाकुलकोश`,
॰ `पाठांशकोश` and `वाक्यदोष`. The import was simply absent: all three members
॰ are declared `सार्वजनिक` over there (`vakyavibhaga.t1:328` for the first), so
॰ nothing was missing except the line that brings the module into scope.
॰
॰ A QUALIFIED NAME WHOSE MODULE IS NOT IMPORTED DOES NOT FAIL AS A MODULE
॰ ERROR. `अर्थ` resolves the prefix against this file's imports, finds none,
॰ and reports the WHOLE WORD as an undeclared name — `वाक्यविभागॱसंज्ञाकुलकोश`
॰ — because the lexer keeps an interior `ॱ` inside the word. So a missing
॰ import and a misspelt name are the same message, and only the shape of the
॰ name tells them apart.
आयातः वाक्यविभाग ।
॰ For निदानपङ्क्तयः 's row walk over spec/diagnostics.tsv — पङ्क्तिसीमा ,
॰ उपेक्ष्यपङ्क्तिः , क्षेत्रसंख्या , क्षेत्रारम्भः and क्षेत्रसीमा . The same
॰ five समयोजन ॱ भेदाङ्कः reads relocations-riscv64.tsv through
॰ (samyojana.t1:501-531), so the crate has ONE table reader and not four.
आयातः सङ्केतन ।
आयातः पदविभाग ।   ॰ the spec-table store: `समावेशपाठः` answers a table by name (2026-09-14)


॰ ══════════════════ UAX #29, the four rules that can fire ══════════════
॰ THE SEGMENTER RETURNS WHICH RULE DECIDED, and that is not decoration.
॰ A code-point segmenter — the defect this row exists to prevent — returns
॰ विच्छेदनियमः and nothing else, forever. Every other module in this crate
॰ that answered the same question answered it this way: मध्यरूप made the
॰ instruction kind the first argument so ir_kinds_built could see it, and
॰ वाक्यविभाग made the statement kind first for the same reason. Here the
॰ RULE is the return value, so a test can count which rules the file
॰ actually applies and name the one that makes क्ष a single अक्षर .

सार्वजनिक चरः योजकनियमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ९ ।       ॰ GB9   — विस्तारः attaches
सार्वजनिक चरः मात्रानियमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ९१ ।    ॰ GB9a  — मात्रा attaches
सार्वजनिक चरः संयोगनियमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ९३ ।     ॰ GB9c  — the conjunct rule
सार्वजनिक चरः विच्छेदनियमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ९९९ ।  ॰ GB999 — otherwise, break

॰ Grapheme_Cluster_Break, restricted to the Devanagari block.
सार्वजनिक चरः अन्यद्वर्गः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।     ॰ GraphemeBreak::Other
सार्वजनिक चरः विस्तारवर्गः ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।    ॰ GraphemeBreak::Extend
सार्वजनिक चरः मात्रावर्गः ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।     ॰ GraphemeBreak::SpacingMark

॰ Indic_Conjunct_Break, likewise. GB9c reads nothing else.
सार्वजनिक चरः अन्तर्नास्ति ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।    ॰ Incb::None
सार्वजनिक चरः अन्तर्व्यञ्जनम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ । ॰ Incb::Consonant
सार्वजनिक चरः अन्तर्योजकम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।    ॰ Incb::Linker — the virāma
सार्वजनिक चरः अन्तर्विस्तारः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।  ॰ Incb::Extend


॰ ══════════════════ UTF-8, one code point at a time ══════════════════
॰ पदविभाग ॱ पदविभाग already walks a source by lead byte to COUNT
॰ akṣaras. Counting needs only the width; deciding a break needs the code
॰ point itself, because every rule above is a range test. So this decodes
॰ where the lexer only measures.

॰ How many अष्टक the sequence beginning with this lead byte occupies.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः अष्टकसंख्या आदाय अग्रिमाष्टक ॱॱ अ८ ददाति न६४ आदि
    यदि अग्रिमाष्टक न्यूनम् १२८ आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् १ ।
    इति
    यदि अग्रिमाष्टक न्यूनम् २२४ आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् २ ।
    इति
    यदि अग्रिमाष्टक न्यूनम् २४० आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ३ ।
    इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् ४ ।
इति

॰ The code point beginning at सूचकाङ्क . Devanagari is the three-अष्टक
॰ case throughout; the other three are written because a comment and a
॰ literal may hold anything the repertoire admits, and a decoder that
॰ handled only its own script would misread the first one it met.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः सङ्केताङ्कः आदाय मूल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ सूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः अग्रिमाष्टक ॱॱ अ८ भवति मूल अङ्कः सूचकाङ्क अन्तः ।
    चरः व्याप्ति ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकसंख्या अग्रिमाष्टक ।

    यदि व्याप्ति समम् १ आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् अग्रिमाष्टक ।
    इति

    यदि व्याप्ति समम् २ आदि
        चरः द्वितीय ॱॱ अ८ भवति मूल अङ्कः आरभ्य सूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् आरभ्य आरभ्य अग्रिमाष्टक वियोगः १९२ समाप्तम् गुणनम् ६४ समाप्तम्
            योगः आरभ्य द्वितीय वियोगः १२८ समाप्तम् ।
    इति

    यदि व्याप्ति समम् ३ आदि
        चरः द्वितीयः ॱॱ अ८ भवति मूल अङ्कः आरभ्य सूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
        चरः तृतीयः ॱॱ अ८ भवति मूल अङ्कः आरभ्य सूचकाङ्क योगः २ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् आरभ्य आरभ्य अग्रिमाष्टक वियोगः २२४ समाप्तम् गुणनम् ४०९६ समाप्तम्
            योगः आरभ्य आरभ्य द्वितीयः वियोगः १२८ समाप्तम् गुणनम् ६४ समाप्तम्
            योगः आरभ्य तृतीयः वियोगः १२८ समाप्तम् ।
    इति

    चरः द्वितीयम् ॱॱ अ८ भवति मूल अङ्कः आरभ्य सूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
    चरः तृतीयम् ॱॱ अ८ भवति मूल अङ्कः आरभ्य सूचकाङ्क योगः २ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
    चरः चतुर्थम् ॱॱ अ८ भवति मूल अङ्कः आरभ्य सूचकाङ्क योगः ३ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् आरभ्य आरभ्य अग्रिमाष्टक वियोगः २४० समाप्तम् गुणनम् २६२१४४ समाप्तम्
        योगः आरभ्य आरभ्य द्वितीयम् वियोगः १२८ समाप्तम् गुणनम् ४०९६ समाप्तम्
        योगः आरभ्य आरभ्य तृतीयम् वियोगः १२८ समाप्तम् गुणनम् ६४ समाप्तम्
        योगः आरभ्य चतुर्थम् वियोगः १२८ समाप्तम् ।
